<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RM_LongShade                                   LONGSHADE_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 step 2

    Copied from src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_Desert.xml (frozen
    the same pass this file was created, see that file's own header) — the source
    of truth being copied, not corrected. Full authoring history (sheet SS0-SS10,
    every ruling behind every field below) stays in that file; do not duplicate it
    here, read it there.

    Changed from the twin, and ONLY this:
      - defName RUT_Desert -> RM_LongShade.
      - label "the Desert" -> "the Long Shade" (biome_mod_architecture.md §7 Q2,
        RULED 2026-09-21 — the owner's own recommended row; the twin keeps its old
        label unchanged, frozen).
      - wildAnimals: the 37 remaining canon Star Wars rows are OUT of this def
        by design (§7 Q11/Q12 — RimMandrake never names Star Wars) and ride
        UtinniPatches/Patches/WildAnimals_LongShade.xml as a PatchOperationAdd
        instead, MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary". JOE_Landopus stays inline
        (MayRequire="mandrake.rut.patches": its def lives in that mod). RM_Qorrax
        (renamed from JOE_Cephalope, Q7 ratified) is native to mandrake.rm.stillsand
        since STILLSAND_BEDAZZLE_CONTENT_1, so its row here carries
        MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes".

        🔴 LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 (2026-09-27 sitting, Q1/Q5/Q6/Q8/Q9)
        landed the sitting's rulings here, same pass as the new
        RM_LongShade_Fauna.xml / RM_LongShade_Gloomcast.xml files:
          - 14 invented-name rows (bokka, ossik, kudda, thurra, vosska,
            khorrak, ommok, ulgga, jellypot, truffle mole, great devourer,
            groundrunner, mature fleshbeast, shade whale) LEFT the Utinni
            patch and now live INLINE below as their own RM_ defs — Q1, all
            14 ratified. Labels unchanged except the shade whale, RULED
            "gloomcast" (Q5).
          - RSW_Kreetle and RSW_Gizka came OUT of the patch's Add block
            entirely — Q6: kreetle's one home is now the Stillsand (reversing
            this doc's own §7 recommendation), gizka's is Pyrelands+Stillsand
            per the existing 2026-09-14 ruling.
          - RSW_Dewback went IN, added to the patch's Add block — Q8:
            herd/mount stock, predator flag MEASURED (RSW_Dewback.xml carries
            no <predator> node at all — defaults false, the roster's "flag
            noise" suspicion confirmed correct), slowed 4.7->4.4 via
            rosters/desert.json stat_adjustments + gen_stat_adjustments.py
            (the wraid/gutkurr treatment). Blurrg stays OUT per Q8's other
            half.
        Net: the patch's Add block is now 37 rows (36 canon + RSW_GlitterBird,
        the whale's commensal, unaffected by this sitting) plus RSW_Dewback.
      - wildPlants: RUT_Vorrel -> RM_Vorrel, MayRequire dropped (moved into this
        mod's own Defs per §7 Q8 — see RM_Vorrel.xml's own header). RM_Leachmoss
        and RM_Venomvine stay inline (non-Star-Wars, this mod's own). 5 of the
        6 RSW_-tier rows found in violation of SW_FAUNA_NEVER_IN_RM_TIER_1
        (audited 2026-09-25) — RSW_SurraGrass, RSW_Plant_Chakroot_Wild,
        RSW_Plant_HubbaGourd_Wild, RSW_VellaraBloom, RSW_DommoTree — ride
        UtinniPatches/Patches/WildAnimals_LongShade.xml as a PatchOperationAdd,
        same shape as the wildAnimals rows above.
        🔴 LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 Q2/Q6: the 6th, RSW_Ultracactus, LEFT
        that patch instead and is now inline as RM_Ultracactus — Q2 ruling
        (owner, typed): "The ultracactus is not canon, I made it." RM_Dewfringe
        (new, Q6) and its harvest RM_DewfringeSprig are inline too, growth
        gated to shade-boundary cells by RM_Patch_DewfringeWildSpawnGate.cs
        (mirrors RM_Leachmoss's own spawn-gate pattern, per-cell instead of a
        global on/off).

    Everything else below — terrain, weather, diseases, allowedPackAnimals,
    wildPlantRegrowDays — is byte-for-byte the twin's own values.
    foragedFood changed by LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 Q3: RSW_RawHubbaGourd
    (MayRequire-guarded, inert standalone — DESERT_FORAGEDFOOD_INERT_1's exact
    defect one tier down) -> RM_UltracactusPad, a real standalone RM-tier item.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RM_LongShade</defName>
    <label>the Long Shade</label>
    <description>A dayside band of scattered rock at a sun so low every stone throws a shadow four times its own height. Nothing lives in the light and nothing survives leaving shelter, so life here is a sprint between islands of shade -- rest, dash, rest -- and the gaps between them are the only geography that matters. Cooler and steadier than the deep dune beyond it: the numbers are small, but they hold.</description>
    <workerClass>RimWorld.BiomeWorker_Desert</workerClass>

    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>false</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>0.4</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.05</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.25</forageability>
    <foragedFood>RM_UltracactusPad</foragedFood>  <!-- LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 Q3: real standalone RM-tier forage, closes the DESERT_FORAGEDFOOD_INERT_1 gap one tier down -->

    <wildPlantsCareAboutLocalFertility>false</wildPlantsCareAboutLocalFertility>
    <lakeBeachTerrain>Sand</lakeBeachTerrain>
    <movementDifficulty>1</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>World/Biomes/Desert</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>90</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>80</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_OrganDecay</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>10</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Sand</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.8</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>Soil</terrain>
        <min>0.8</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <!-- DEEP_SAND_WALKABLE_TERRAIN_1 — owner, 2026-09-27: "an entire terrain type,
         not just small pools. Some in the Long Shade, Muchly in the Stillsand."
         Mechanism reused verbatim from vanilla Desert/ExtremeDesert's own SoftSand
         patch (Defs/Core/BiomeDefs/Biomes_WarmArid.xml — this biome's own donor
         twin already ships one at perlinFrequency 0.05/threshold min 0.65/minSize
         13); this is the same TerrainPatchMaker vanilla already uses to paint a
         regional secondary terrain over terrainsByFertility, not a new GenStep.
         "Some" = the SAME threshold vanilla uses for a modest, scattered presence
         (min 0.65 — a proven "minority terrain" number), with minSize raised well
         past vanilla's 13 so a qualifying patch always reads as a region, never a
         one-cell speck (see RM_Stillsand_Biome.xml's own comment for the "Muchly"
         side of this same tuning). -->
    <terrainPatchMakers>
      <li>
        <perlinFrequency>0.045</perlinFrequency>
        <minSize>60</minSize>
        <thresholds>
          <li>
            <terrain>RM_DeepSand</terrain>
            <min>0.65</min>
            <max>999</max>
          </li>
        </thresholds>
      </li>
    </terrainPatchMakers>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>90</Clear>
      <DryThunderstorm>4</DryThunderstorm>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <GrayPall MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">1</GrayPall>
      <Sandstorm MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">4</Sandstorm>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <JOE_Landopus MayRequire="mandrake.rut.patches">0.5</JOE_Landopus>  <!-- landopus - small ambush predator, this biome's own native fauna -->
      <RM_Qorrax MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">0.5</RM_Qorrax>  <!-- qorrax (was JOE_Cephalope, LONGSHADE_BEDAZZLE_CONTENT_1 part 3, Q7 ratified) - sand burrower & swimmer, this biome's own native fauna -->
      <!-- LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 Q1/Q5: the 14 invented-name rows, moved
           inline from the Utinni patch this pass. Weights carried over
           verbatim from WildAnimals_LongShade.xml's own Add block. -->
      <RM_Bokka>0.5</RM_Bokka>
      <RM_Ossik>0.4</RM_Ossik>
      <RM_Kudda>0.2</RM_Kudda>
      <RM_Thurra>0.05</RM_Thurra>
      <RM_Vosska>0.05</RM_Vosska>
      <RM_Khorrak>0.035</RM_Khorrak>
      <RM_Ommok>0.025</RM_Ommok>
      <RM_Ulgga>0.015</RM_Ulgga>
      <RM_Jellypot>0.7</RM_Jellypot>
      <RM_TruffleMole>0.5</RM_TruffleMole>
      <RM_GreatDevourer>0.5</RM_GreatDevourer>
      <RM_Groundrunner>0.5</RM_Groundrunner>
      <RM_MatureFleshbeast>0.5</RM_MatureFleshbeast>
      <RM_Gloomcast>0.015</RM_Gloomcast>  <!-- the shade whale, RULED "gloomcast" (Q5) -->
      <!-- LONGSHADE_BEDAZZLE_CONTENT_1 part 2: the four Q4-ruled fillers
           (sollak/gennok/tebbra/dakkra), RM_LongShade_Fillers.xml. Commonalities
           follow the same size-vs-rarity pyramid as the rest of this list —
           sollak is the only one of the four over bs 2. -->
      <RM_Sollak>0.1</RM_Sollak>
      <RM_Gennok>0.3</RM_Gennok>
      <RM_Tebbra>0.6</RM_Tebbra>
      <RM_Dakkra>0.05</RM_Dakkra>
      <!-- LONGSHADE_BEDAZZLE_CONTENT_1 part 4: RM_Pirrik, the merge of the
           sitting's "pirrik" filler and RSW_GlitterBird (retired, was patch-
           added at the same 0.2 weight from WildAnimals_LongShade.xml — see
           that file's header). Inline here, not behind the Utinni patch
           layer, per Q11a: "glitter-bird" is descriptive English, not canon
           Star Wars IP. -->
      <RM_Pirrik>0.2</RM_Pirrik>
      <!-- LONGSHADE_BEDAZZLE_MECHANICS_1 tranche 2: the mirrak, the false-shadow
           ambusher (RM_LongShade_Mirrak.xml), wired once its art landed. 0.05 is
           the dakkra's weight, the other rare ambusher; a first value. -->
      <RM_Mirrak>0.05</RM_Mirrak>
      <!-- The 36 remaining canon Star Wars rows (§7 Q11/Q12) ride
           WildAnimals_LongShade.xml as a PatchOperationAdd instead of living
           here — see this file's header. -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <RM_Leachmoss>1.5</RM_Leachmoss>  <!-- leachmoss: the fertile ground's fastest claimant, DESERT_LEACHMOSS_BUILD_1. -->
      <RM_Vorrel>0.1</RM_Vorrel>  <!-- the cycle plant, moved+renamed from RUT_Vorrel per §7 Q8, this mod's own def now, no MayRequire needed. Working name, see RM_Vorrel.xml's own header. -->
      <RM_Venomvine>0.25</RM_Venomvine>  <!-- the vine that holds territory by injury, VENOMVINE_CONTACT_VENOM_BUILD_1. -->
      <RM_Ultracactus>0.8</RM_Ultracactus>  <!-- LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 Q2: moved inline, weight carried over verbatim from the Utinni patch's Add block. "The ultracactus is not canon, I made it." -->
      <RM_Dewfringe>0.4</RM_Dewfringe>  <!-- LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 Q6: new shade-boundary rim plant, growth gated to the rim by RM_Patch_DewfringeWildSpawnGate.cs — this weight only matters where the C# gate already says yes. -->
      <!-- The 5 remaining RSW_-tier rows (SW_FAUNA_NEVER_IN_RM_TIER_1) ride
           WildAnimals_LongShade.xml as a PatchOperationAdd instead of living
           here — see this file's header. -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>35</wildPlantRegrowDays>

    <!-- LONGSHADE_BEDAZZLE_MECHANICS_1 tranche 2: the Crawler Road (§6.4) and the
         Long Carry's sun graves (§6.5). Named here only, so they run on this biome
         alone. RM_LongShade_GenSteps.xml; toggles in this mod's settings. -->
    <extraGenSteps>
      <li>RM_GenStep_CrawlerRoad</li>
      <li>RM_GenStep_SunGraves</li>
    </extraGenSteps>

    <allowedPackAnimals>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Bantha</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Ronto</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Eopie</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Jamel</li>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_Falumpaset</li>
    </allowedPackAnimals>

    <!-- LONGSHADE_BEDAZZLE_MECHANICS_1 part 1 — the golden hour (owner: "I like
         the golden hour concept. A perpetual beautiful sunset."). A pinned sun:
         one fixed sunset sky that never turns to night, and one fixed shadow
         vector every rock, wall and tree renders along, pointing away from the
         substellar point (Ash'karr's is 0,0). The same vector is exposed to the
         directional shade grid (SOLAR_HEAT_EXPOSURE_1) so the rendered shadows
         and the mechanical shade agree. Mechanism and toggle live in
         mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors (RM_MapComponent_PinnedSun,
         "Pinned sun (golden hour)" in its Mod Settings). Colours and glow are
         first values — tuned by looking, in game, with the owner. -->
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_PinnedSunExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">
        <substellarLatitude>0</substellarLatitude>
        <substellarLongitude>0</substellarLongitude>
        <minElevationDegrees>2</minElevationDegrees>
        <maxElevationDegrees>30</maxElevationDegrees>
        <glow>0.8</glow>
        <skyColor>(1, 0.80, 0.62)</skyColor>
        <shadowColor>(0.52, 0.48, 0.72)</shadowColor>
        <overlayColor>(1, 0.86, 0.70)</overlayColor>
        <saturation>1.1</saturation>
        <lightsourceShineSize>2.5</lightsourceShineSize>
        <lightsourceShineIntensity>0.8</lightsourceShineIntensity>
        <shadowStrength>1</shadowStrength>
      </li>
      <!-- SOLAR_HEAT_EXPOSURE_1: sun heat kind "overhead" - the Long Shade: owner ruling, longshade_shade_ideation_2026-09-29.md "overhead sun here, so parasols and tents work".
           heatOffsetC is an invented first value; the owner-watched sitting tunes it. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_SunHeatExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">
        <heatKind>overhead</heatKind>
        <heatOffsetC>30</heatOffsetC>
      </li>
      <!-- LONGSHADE_GPT_ENRICHMENT_1 §3, heat you can hear: lit vs shade bed at the
           camera's cell (owner: "It's ok for the heat sound to be where the camera is
           rather than your people."). Sounds: ../SoundDefs/RM_LongShade_HeatSounds.xml
           (placeholder audio). Toggles: Creature Behaviors, "Heat you can hear" and
           "Herd calls and giant footfalls". Numbers are the extension's TUNED defaults. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_HeatSoundscapeExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">
        <litSound>RM_Heat_LitBed</litSound>
        <shadeSound>RM_Heat_ShadeBed</shadeSound>
      </li>
      <!-- LONGSHADE_GPT_ENRICHMENT_1 §1, Shipfall Commons (Source/RM_ShipfallCommons.cs).
           The rung ORDER is the item's spec, verbatim in sense: "small animals take the
           ramp shadow, herds press the hull, pirrik circle, eventually the gloomcast
           walks over". TUNED: every delay, the 0.7 "small" body size, the radius and the
           chances are first values; no ruling gives them. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.LongShade.RM_ShipfallCommonsExtension">
        <radius>8</radius>
        <minShade>0.5</minShade>
        <pullChance>0.3</pullChance>
        <stayChance>0.8</stayChance>
        <dispersalDistance>30</dispersalDistance>
        <dispersalMessage>The animals sheltering in the ship's shade scatter as the engine wakes.</dispersalMessage>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <afterHours>2</afterHours>
            <maxBodySize>0.7</maxBodySize>
            <message>Small animals have crept into the shade of the ship.</message>
          </li>
          <li>
            <afterHours>8</afterHours>
            <herdOnly>true</herdOnly>
            <message>Herds are pressing against the hull, out of the sun.</message>
          </li>
          <li>
            <afterHours>16</afterHours>
            <races>
              <li>RM_Pirrik</li>
            </races>
            <walk>true</walk>
            <message>Pirrik are circling over the ship's shadow.</message>
          </li>
          <li>
            <afterHours>36</afterHours>
            <races>
              <li>RM_Gloomcast</li>
            </races>
            <walk>true</walk>
            <message>A gloomcast has turned toward the ship.</message>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
